# Organisation lifecycle & tenancy invariant

Canonical: `docs/foundations/ORGANISATION-LIFECYCLE.md`

## The invariant (locked)

**Authentication establishes identity. Membership establishes tenant context. Explicit onboarding creates a tenant.**

A Clerk identity with no membership is a valid **memberless / onboarding** state. Never turn it into a tenant.

## Never create an organisation during

Clerk authentication · `user.created` webhook · session resolution · middleware · dashboard/page loading · sign-up · onboarding · user synchronisation · normal login/refresh · invite claiming when there is no invitation.

Do **not** reintroduce `provisionOrganisation` or any implicit/fallback organisation creation to "fix" a missing membership.

## Only intentional creation boundaries (allowlist)

- `createOrganisationForUser` — explicit `POST /api/v1/org/create`
- `createClientOrganisation` — operator-only prospect→client conversion (`PlatformOperatorContext`)
- `ensureWantdOrganisation` — manual `scripts/ensure-wantd-org.mjs` (singleton Wantd marketplace)
- demo/seed tooling

Any new `prisma.organisation.create` outside these fails `scripts/test-organisation-lifecycle.mjs`.

## Team invitations

`claimTeamInvitesForUser` activates an **existing** invited membership in an **existing** organisation. With no pending invite and no `organisationId` it returns `null` and creates nothing. Do not break invite claiming; do not let it create an organisation.

## Active org

`dg_active_org` is a browser cookie, not a DB value. An active-org pointing at an org the identity is not a member of must be ignored — never resolved by creating an organisation.
